  "notes": "USAGE:\n{脱走|だっそう}する is used for escaping from confinement or a place where one is obligated to remain. It implies unauthorized departure, distinguishing it from simply leaving.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {脱走|だっそう}する (to escape, to desert)\n- {脱走|だっそう}{犯|はん} (escaped convict)\n- {脱走|だっそう}{兵|へい} (deserter — military)\n- {脱走|だっそう}{経路|けいろ} (escape route)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{逃亡|とうぼう} emphasizes fleeing and going into hiding, while {脱走|だっそう} emphasizes the act of breaking free from confinement. {脱獄|だつごく} specifically means escaping from prison.",
